# Offline synthetic artifacts exercise comparison presentation; no model is called.
name: Exact source revisions and honest nondeterministic absence
size: 120x36
cwd: @TMP_TARGET
env-unset: ANTHROPIC_API_KEY OPENAI_API_KEY NO_COLOR
env: KUZUSHI_SKIP_ONBOARDING=1 KUZUSHI_REDUCED_MOTION=1
shell: python3 @REPO/scripts/devex/fixtures/revision_comparison.py @TMP_TARGET
launch: --target @TMP_TARGET
require-live-snap: 30 KUZUSHI | shell-ready
submit: runs diff fixture-base fixture-later
require-live-snap: 20 1 not observed | revision-comparison
expect: rev:aaaaaaa*
expect: content:bbbb
expect: content:cccc
expect: 1 not observed
expect: 1 not reassessed
expect: 1 seen again
expect: Absence does not establish a fix.
ask: Can the operator distinguish the same SHA with two content hashes and understand that absence does not prove a fix?
nav-mode:
keys: NPage
live-snap: comparison-coverage
expect: NOT OBSERVED IN COVERED WORK
expect: NOT REASSESSED IN RIGHT
expect: outside the recorded scan scope
ask: Are both absence categories readable and reachable by keyboard, with the uncovered finding's reason visible?
keys: C-c
